    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0550" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg466"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. White reports that Lord Lansdowne handed him a note<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d457-f1"/> agreeing that Mr. Bowen, as representative of Venezuela,
                    shall confer with the British ambassador at Washington, provided definite
                    assurance is received that the Venezuelan Government accepts the conditions laid
                    down in the memorandum of December 23, 1902.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
